 "remarks": "Tucked behind classic stone walls topped with fencing on almost 2 private, flat acres, this fully renovated 1900 Colonial pairs original character and charm with modern ease, minutes from Wilton Town Center and Wilton's award-winning schools. The chef's kitchen is a showpiece, flooded with natural light and anchored by an oversized island made for gathering. Limestone counters, Sub-Zero and Viking range complete the space, while a slider opens to a deck with sweeping views of the picturesque backyard. Main-level laundry is nearby, and easy access to the stone patios makes entertaining effortless. Dinners feel like an occasion in the dining room, with a huge bay window and fireplace. The oversized family room is the heart of the home, with vaulted ceilings, antique barn beams and a stone fireplace. A den off it works as an office or playroom. Upstairs, 4 bedrooms include a primary suite with a newly renovated bath. The 3rd floor, with full bath and storage, adds approx. 400 sq ft (not in listed sq ft) for a playroom, office, gym or guest space. Out back, 2 multi-level stone patios open to a flat, dry, fully enclosed yard with room for kids and pets to play. Quality details include James Hardie siding and trim, copper gutters, Marvin windows and a 10-year-young septic.",
